kings/theory/LOOPY.md:76:| R2.11 | GAP → PROVED in P (frozen), as a sufficient condition (revised after K10, 2026-10-22): Proposition 2.11 and Corollary 2.11a give (V2) at a passer or race terminal under (H1)–(H5): a clear path for pawns and kings of both colours, no check, no stalemate, no interference of an ω pawn that captures a β pawn on a neighbouring file, and the timing bound for both move orders over all ω pawns. K10's first draft was FALSE (it ignored all of these); the statement and proof were rebuilt by a Sonnet agent and read step by step by the integrator. One AI proof, checked on 954,392 parked and 60,000 random-king positions with side to move against `kpsolve --frozen` (0 violations; scripts in `kings/delegate/out/K10/scripts/`). Computation CHECKED-2 by K10v (independent code, opencode beam-free): 0 violations in 146,328 certified instances (an instance is a position, side to move, β and p; 119,654 distinct positions with side to move) and 5,716 with an e.p. right; its proof verdict SOUND has no written derivation, so the proof is not re-derived by a second model (revised after K10v, 2026-10-22). Second round: two fresh Sonnet reviewers read the proof and found no error, and their own code found 0 violations in 5,730,596 certified positions with side to move (6,783,482 instances) on cylinders, plus 434,429 positions on flat boards, also 0 violations; no model outside the Sonnet family has re-derived it (revised after the K10 second round, 2026-10-22). Real kings: nothing proved, the square rule is a CONJECTURE (scratch evidence) | R3 item 6; K10 |
kings/theory/LOOPY.md:103:| P11 | PROVED in P, in conditional form (revised after K10, 2026-10-22): `--frozen` = o(W(X)) for every X of the layout whose passer and race terminals are all certified: by Corollary 2.11a at every node reached by a move and, if X already has a passer (then W(X) ends at the root), by Proposition 2.11 at X itself, with s the side to move and β the side that W(X) credits. Without the root clause the claim is false: `Ka1 ka6 Pc2 Pd4 pd3 b -` is a White win in W(X) and (L, L) in `--frozen` (revised after the K10 second round). The chain is Theorem 1.14(i) with (V1) from the layout (no check is possible, and a king move is always legal) and condition (E) of L1.6 in `notes/lemmas.md`, (V3) by fiat, and (V2) by fiat at king moves, by Corollary 2.11a at every passer and race terminal reached by a move, and by Proposition 2.11 at a root that already has a passer; the o(S) clause adds HSS with Theorem 1.11(c) and Theorem 1.14(ii). Without the certificate the equality is FALSE (`Ka1 ka6 Pc2 Pc3 pd3 pd4 w -`: o(W) is a White win, `--frozen` is (L, L)). The root clause is swept (revised after K12, 2026-10-27): on the layout (Ka1, Black's king at the top of the a-file, pawns on files c to W − 2, both sides to move, legal e.p. rights included) of cyl:6×6 and cyl:7×6 with ≤ 3 pawns a side and cyl:8×6 with ≤ 2, there are 716,962 roots with a passer; no certified root disagrees with `--frozen`, and the 20,376 roots where W(X) is wrong are all uncertified, so the clause is what excludes them (COMPUTED-1, `kings/delegate/out/K12/`). On cyl:6×6 (≤ 3 a side) and cyl:8×6 (≤ 2 a side) without e.p. rights the integrator re-ran the sweep with separate code (its own root generator, credit from `cylcgt`, `kpsolve --frozen`, and the K10r2 hypothesis checker): the same 76,744 and 68,036 roots, 0 certified disagreements (CHECKED-2 there; `kings/delegate/out/K12/REVIEW.md`). Controls: dropping (H4) gives 48 certified violations, weakening (H5) 15,868. Not yet done: P11's own harness does not test (H4) and (H5) (the K10 end-to-end script `kings/delegate/out/K10/scripts/e2e.py` does, on the roots listed under Proposition 2.11), and no model outside the Sonnet family has re-derived Proposition 2.11 (in the K10 second round two fresh Sonnet reviewers found no error) | R1 item 11; K10 |
