kings/delegate/logs/K10v.log:2208:- **Corollary 2.11a vs `_child`:** matches exactly. With mover M and side to move N at the terminal: only M passed → b = M; only N passed → b = N; race under the count rule → b = N iff dp(N) ≤ dp(M), else b = M. This is precisely `_child`'s `RACE_RULE == "count"` branch (and the only-M / only-N cases follow from `value`). The e values are e = d when b = M (opponent moves first) and e = d − 1 when b = N (beneficiary moves first).
