kings/delegate/out/K10v/REPORT.md:16:5. Recommend upgrading Proposition 2.11, and the (V2) part of P11, from PROVED to CHECKED-2 in the frozen model.
kings/delegate/out/K10v/REPORT.md:20:All of F1–F3, Step 1 (king safety), Step 2 (invariant under β move, ω push, double step, capture into the strip from outside, capture out of the strip, and the e.p. capture offered at y), Step 3 (consequences), Step 4 (every real ω move is a move of G_ω, so k ≥ μ_ω), and Step 5 (timing for both move orders, e = d or d − 1) are **SOUND**. No missing step or counterexample found.
kings/delegate/out/K10v/REPORT.md:22:- **Corollary 2.11a vs `_child`:** matches exactly. With mover M and side to move N at the terminal: only M passed → b = M; only N passed → b = N; race under the count rule → b = N iff dp(N) ≤ dp(M), else b = M. This is precisely `_child`'s `RACE_RULE == "count"` branch (and the only-M / only-N cases follow from `value`). The e values are e = d when b = M (opponent moves first) and e = d − 1 when b = N (beneficiary moves first).
kings/delegate/out/K10v/REPORT.md:23:- **Corollary 2.11b (cyl:8×6, Ka1 ka6, pawns on c–g):** verified computationally for both colours: (H2) and (H3) hold, and no king stands on p's file. Only the passed front pawn, (H4) and (H5) need checking.
kings/delegate/out/K10v/REPORT.md:66:- **P11:** upgrade the (V2) certificate part to **CHECKED-2** (frozen model), still conditional on (E) and hereditary sum-safety as before.
