kings/delegate/logs/K11.log:1671:76:| R2.11 | GAP → PROVED in P (frozen), as a sufficient condition (revised after K10, 2026-10-22): Proposition 2.11 and Corollary 2.11a give (V2) at a passer or race terminal under (H1)–(H5): a clear path for pawns and kings of both colours, no check, no stalemate, no interference of an ω pawn that captures a β pawn on a neighbouring file, and the timing bound for both move orders over all ω pawns. K10's first draft was FALSE (it ignored all of these); the statement and proof were rebuilt by a Sonnet agent and read step by step by the integrator. One AI proof, checked on 954,392 parked and 60,000 random-king positions with side to move against `kpsolve --frozen` (0 violations; scripts in `kings/delegate/out/K10/scripts/`). Computation CHECKED-2 by K10v (independent code, opencode beam-free): 0 violations in 146,328 certified instances (an instance is a position, side to move, β and p; 119,654 distinct positions with side to move) and 5,716 with an e.p. right; its proof verdict SOUND has no written derivation, so the proof is not re-derived by a second model (revised after K10v, 2026-10-22). Second round: two fresh Sonnet reviewers read the proof and found no error, and their own code found 0 violations in 5,730,596 certified positions with side to move (6,783,482 instances) on cylinders, plus 434,429 positions on flat boards, also 0 violations; no model outside the Sonnet family has re-derived it (revised after the K10 second round, 2026-10-22). Real kings: nothing proved, the square rule is a CONJECTURE (scratch evidence) | R3 item 6; K10 |
