kings/delegate/out/K10/REPORT.md:116:With frozen kings, (V1) (non-interaction, no stalemate) holds by the harness's condition (E) and its layout check, and (V3) (every Z-move is a suicide) holds by fiat (a king move loses at once). The remaining gap was (V2) for passer terminals: Theorem 2.7 covers punished king moves, but passers were only "speed-certified" (Remark 2.11, previously GAP). Proposition 2.11 (this task) now supplies (V2) for passer terminals under frozen kings, with the bound μ ≥ d + 1 and the clear-path/stalemate conditions that the harness checks. Theorem 1.11 supplies the sum. HSS supplies o(S) = o(D). (A_Q) is not involved, because P11 is a P-level statement (it compares --frozen, a P-computation, with o(W) and o(S), both P-level). Hence the backing is complete in P, and P11 is no longer GAP.
