kings/delegate/out/K11/REPORT.md:67:I checked the tempting false one-liner noted in Step 2 explicitly: a capture of a β pawn on a neighbouring file does put an ω pawn into the strip, and (H4) is exactly the bound that saves the invariant. This matches the first K10 error (a capture of a β pawn on a neighbouring file lets an ω pawn stop the passer).
kings/delegate/out/K11/REPORT.md:73:**Corollary 2.11a.** At a node y′ reached by a move of M, with N to move, cylcgt credits the terminal to b as follows: only M has a passed pawn ⇒ b = M; only N ⇒ b = N; both (a race, count rule) ⇒ b = N if dp(N) ≤ dp(M), else b = M. This is exactly cylcgt's `_child` race rule (winner = the opponent of the mover when the opponent's `promote_distance` ≤ the mover's). The corollary applies Proposition 2.11 at (y′, s = N, β = b), with e = d if b = M and e = d − 1 if b = N, covering both move orders and a race won by the side to move. **Verdict: SOUND**, and it matches the code.
kings/delegate/out/K11/REPORT.md:75:**Corollary 2.11b.** On cyl:8×6 with `Ka1 ka6` and pawns only on c–g: pawns stay on c–g (F1). For either colour as β, (H2) holds (the neighbours of the a-file are b and h, and no pawn stands there); (H3) holds with t = a5 for ω = Black and t = a2 for ω = White (king distance 4 ≥ 2, and the files around t are pawn-free). So at a terminal only the passed front pawn, (H4) and (H5) must be checked. A pawn on the a-file breaks (H3) (`Ka1 ka6 Pa3 Pc2 w -` has no neighbour of a6 with three pawn-free files). **Verdict: SOUND**, and the second-round reviewers reproduced (H2),(H3) and the king clause of (H1) in all 371,250 instances on cyl:8×6 with pawns on c–g.
kings/delegate/out/K11/REPORT.md:79:## 4. P11 as now amended
kings/delegate/out/K11/REPORT.md:81:**Does Theorem 1.14(i) + Corollary 2.11a at every terminal reached by a move + Proposition 2.11 at a root that already has a passer prove `--frozen` = o(W(X))?** Yes, in conditional form. The chain is:
kings/delegate/out/K11/REPORT.md:85:- (V1) holds in the layout by Corollary 2.11b: no check is possible and a king move is always legal (a2 or a5 is available); condition (E) of L1.6 governs en passant.
kings/delegate/out/K11/REPORT.md:86:- (V2) (decisiveness) holds by fiat at king moves (a frozen king move loses at once, a P-win for the opponent), by Corollary 2.11a at every passer and race terminal reached by a move, and by Proposition 2.11 at a root that already has a passer (s = side to move, β = the side W(X) credits).
kings/delegate/out/K11/REPORT.md:92:- A root that already has a passer (including races): covered formally by the root clause, but there is no end-to-end sweep over such roots. P11's harness (56,872 roots) explicitly excludes passers at the root. This is the gap the second round found; it rests on Proposition 2.11 itself plus one counterexample.
kings/delegate/out/K11/REPORT.md:93:- A root with an e.p. right: Proposition 2.11 handles an e.p. capture offered at y, and condition (E) is part of (V1), but roots carrying an e.p. right have been certified only at the instance level (K10v: 5,716 instances, 0 violations), not end to end through P11.
kings/delegate/out/K11/REPORT.md:94:- A root where the side to move is in check: in the `Ka1 ka6` layout this cannot happen — (H2) rules out pawn checks and the kings are distance 4 apart — so it is not a live case for P11, but it is a hypothesis of Theorem 1.14(i) that must be checked per layout.
kings/delegate/out/K11/REPORT.md:132:**Counts from the literature checks I rely on (not re-run by me in full):** K10 parked sweep 954,392 positions, 0 violations; K10v independent 146,328 instances (5,716 with an e.p. right), 0 violations; K10 second round 5,730,596 certified positions with side to move (6,783,482 instances) on cylinders plus 434,429 flat positions, 0 violations. P11 end-to-end: 56,872 roots, 48,000 conservative wins and 26,014 fully certified roots, 0 violations; 3,194 roots differ when some terminal is uncertified; 8 violations when (H4) is dropped.
kings/delegate/out/K11/REPORT.md:140:- **P11:** PROVED in P, in conditional form: `--frozen` = o(W(X)) for every X of the layout whose passer and race terminals are all certified, plus the root clause for roots that already have a passer. The root-with-passer clause (including races and e.p. rights) is not yet swept end to end, so P11 should keep its conditional label and record that verification item; it is not a proof gap, because Proposition 2.11 supplies the certificate. Without the certificate the equality is FALSE, as the two counterexamples show.
